igation is the result of Cary Huﬀman [14] which\n\ngives a decomposition for a linear code as a direct sum of two subcodes related to an automorphism\n\nof the code which has odd order.\n\nThe main results of the paper are the following theorems.\n\nTheorem 1.1. For a positive integer n and k∈ {1,2,3,4, n −4, n −3, n −2, n −1}, there is no\n\nk-dimensional binary linear code C of length n where PAut(C) = h σ i and σ is a ﬁxed point free\n\npermutation of order 3.\n\nTheorem 1.2. For a positive integer n, let σ be a ﬁxed point free permutation of order 3 in S n.\n\nThere is no binary 5-dimensional linear code C of length n≥30 such that PAut(C)is generated\n\nby σ.\n\nThe structure of the paper is as follows. In section 2, we introduce some notations and discuss\n\nlower dimensional cases. In section 3, we present the proofs of the main results.\n\nDate: February 19, 2024.\n\n2010 Mathematics Subject Classiﬁcation. 94B05, 11T71, 20B05.\n\nKey words and phrases. binary linear code, ﬁxed point free permutation automorphism, ﬁxed subcode associated\n\nto a permutation automorphism.\n\n1\n\n2. Notation and results for lower dimensions\n\nA binary linear code of length n and dimension k is a k-dimensional subspace of the vector\n\nspace F n\n\n2. The symmetric group S n acts on F n\n\n2 as follows. For σ∈S n and for v=v 1 v 2. . . v n, we\n\ndeﬁne v σ=v σ−1(1)v σ−1(2) ...v σ−1(n). A permutation automorphism of C is a permutation σ∈S n\n\nsuch that C σ=C. The set of all automorphisms of C forms a subgroup of S n, which is called the\n\npermutation automorphism group of C and it is denoted by PAut(C).\n\nLet C be a binary linear code. Assume that σ is a ﬁxed point free permutation of order 3\n\nin PAut(C). In this case, it is clear that C has length a multiple of 3. So for the rest of the\n\npaper, we assume that C is a binary linear code of length n= 3 m where m is a positive integer.\n\nSince any conjugate of a permutation automorphism of C is a permutation automorphism of